{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>So.</b> The exile of Cush, who came to their aid." "<b>And the exposed.</b> Because the prophet went naked, or HaShem exposed them." "<b>Buttocks.</b> It is the posterior; the form is until their buttocks (2 Samuel 10:4)." "<b>The nakedness of Egypt.</b> This is the nakedness of Egypt, or the word וחשופי שת draws itself and another with it."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {2 "Reading גזרת as referring to the cut/form of the word שת; the syntax is compressed and the exact sense is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:28.769382956Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}